  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let $f(x)$ be positive and strictly increasing for $x\\in [1,4],$ and differentiable for $x\\in (1,4).$ Suppose we approximate the area under the curve $y=g(x)=x\\cdot f(x)$ over the interval $[1,4]$ using a left Riemann sum. Given that $g(x)>0,$ which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. ${f}^{′}(x)>0$\n\nII. ${g}^{′}(x)>0$\n\nIII. The Riemann sum underestimates the true area.",
